A||||2||merlin||Partial Wheel refinishing||||5||
Z||000000||merlin||01-21-2001||12:19 PM||||I’m planning on refinishing my ‘honeycomb’ rims on my 87 GT next month and I have read a few threads and website articles, but I still have two questions. <P>1. The stock gray paint on my rims aren’t that bad and I could probably bring back the finish with some rubbing compound.  However, the silver/chrome circumference of the wheel is bad.  Is it possible to refinish that part of the wheel without damaging the gray center.<BR>2. Has anyone refinished the wheels with the tires still on the wheel? <BR>||||reg||5
Z||000001||Mark||01-21-2001||12:27 PM||||Yes to both questions.  If you use a chemical stripper to remove the clearcoat on the rim part, just mask off the center of the wheel, carefully apply the stripper (this is where the gel type stripper works well), and scrape/wash it off as soon as the old finish wrinkles.  Likewise, avoid getting the stripper on the rubber.  If you do, just wipe it off with a damp cloth or sponge.  I used a small paint brush to accurately apply the stripper. Just be careful and neat....and don't forget to wear safety glasses!!!<p>[This message has been edited by Mark (edited 01-21-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||fropuff||01-21-2001||02:25 PM||||I did that exact same thing last summer.  I used a spray plastic chemical stripper.  It is called Bulldog plastic chemical stripper or something like that, and it comes in a yellow can with a Bulldog on the front.  I found it at the local paint supplier.  I also got some stuff from NAPA; it's called Plastic parts stripper.  It doesn't work as good as the Bulldog.  Anyway, I masked the painted part off and sprayed it on.  I left it on for about 20 minutes.  I then pressure washed and wiped it off.  I had to do a few coats for the "inner" part of it.  I used a paint brush for that; then used a wood shim to get it out; then pressure washed it.  I'm going to redo my wheels and ground FX this summer, so I'm going to strip everything off.  Bulldog is the way to go!  <P>------------------<BR>Fuzz busters are for those who are worried about being caught.||||reg||1
